    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0223" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4737/36.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of Brazil to
                        President Taft.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-01-18"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 18,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Cordially thank you for condolences which in your name and that of the American
                    people you were so good as to send me on the occasion of the death of Ambassador
                    Joaquim Nabuco.</p>
                <p>The Brazilian Nation and its Government receive with keen appreciation the
                    demonstrations of sympathy with which the United States of America join us in
                    our great grief over the loss that Brazil and the cause of Pan Americanism have
                    just suffered.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nilo Pecanha.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
